  "id": "nn_msgcs20w_wk2f5xr4w",
  "title": "fastapi notes",
  "content": "<h1>PART 1 — Start the FastAPI Project 🚀</h1><p>We are officially starting the <strong>hands-on course</strong>.</p><p>I want you to have VS Code open and follow me exactly. <strong>Do not create the whole project at once.</strong> We will build it step-by-step.</p><hr><h2>Step 1 — Create the project folder</h2><p>Create a new folder anywhere convenient.</p><p>Name it:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi-issue-tracker\n</code></pre></div><p>Then open this folder in <strong>VS Code</strong>.</p><p>Your VS Code should currently look roughly like:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi-issue-tracker/\n</code></pre></div><p>Nothing else yet.</p><hr><h2>Step 2 — Open the terminal</h2><p>In VS Code:</p><p><strong>Terminal → New Terminal</strong></p><p>You should see a terminal opened at your project location.</p><p>Check that you're inside the project folder.</p><p>Run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">pwd</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>On Windows, you can use:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">cd</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>You should see the path of your <code>fastapi-issue-tracker</code> folder.</p><hr><h2>Step 3 — Create a virtual environment</h2><p>Run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">python -m venv .venv\n</code></pre></div><h3>What did we just do?</h3><p>We asked Python:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">python\n  ↓\nrun the venv module\n  ↓\ncreate a virtual environment\n  ↓\ncall it .venv\n</code></pre></div><p>Your project should now look like:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi-issue-tracker/\n│\n└── .venv/\n</code></pre></div><h3>Why do we need this?</h3><p>Imagine you have:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Project A → FastAPI version X\nProject B → FastAPI version Y\n</code></pre></div><p>If everything is installed globally, the projects can interfere with each other.</p><p>A virtual environment gives each project its own Python packages.</p><p>Think:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Your computer\n│\n├── Project A\n│   └── its packages\n│\n├── Project B\n│   └── its packages\n│\n└── Project C\n    └── its packages\n</code></pre></div><p>This is standard backend project practice.</p><hr><h2>Step 4 — Activate the virtual environment</h2><h3>macOS / Linux</h3><p>Run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">source</span> .venv/bin/activate\n</code></pre></div><h3>Windows</h3><p>Run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">.venv\\Scripts\\activate\n</code></pre></div><p>After activation, your terminal should show something similar to:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">(.venv)\n</code></pre></div><p>at the beginning.</p><p>For example:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">(.venv) user@computer fastapi-issue-tracker %\n</code></pre></div><p>That means:</p><blockquote><p><strong>This terminal is now using this project's Python environment.</strong></p></blockquote><hr><h2>Step 5 — Install FastAPI</h2><p>Now run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">pip install <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"fastapi[standard]\"</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>This follows the crash course's setup: the <code>standard</code> extra installs the standard FastAPI tooling needed for the course, including the development server and documentation-related dependencies.</p><p>Wait until installation finishes.</p><p>Then run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">pip list\n</code></pre></div><p>You should see FastAPI and its dependencies.</p><hr><h1>Step 6 — Create <code>main.py</code></h1><p>In the VS Code Explorer:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi-issue-tracker/\n│\n├── .venv/\n│\n└── main.py\n</code></pre></div><p>Open <code>main.py</code>.</p><p>Write <strong>only this</strong>:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> fastapi <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> FastAPI\n</code></pre></div><p>Stop here for a second.</p><h3>What does this mean?</h3><p>We are importing the <code>FastAPI</code> class from the <code>fastapi</code> package.</p><p>Conceptually:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi package\n      │\n      └── FastAPI\n</code></pre></div><p>We're saying:</p><blockquote><p>\"Python, give me the FastAPI class because I want to create a FastAPI application.\"</p></blockquote><hr><h1>Step 7 — Create our application</h1><p>Under it, write:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> fastapi <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n</code></pre></div><p>Now let's understand this line properly:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">app = FastAPI()\n</code></pre></div><p><code>FastAPI()</code> creates our <strong>FastAPI application object</strong>.</p><p>We store that object in:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">app\n</code></pre></div><p>So mentally:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">FastAPI()\n    ↓\ncreates application\n    ↓\napp\n</code></pre></div><p>Later, this <code>app</code> object is what we'll use for things like:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.get(<span class=\"hljs-params\">...</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.post(<span class=\"hljs-params\">...</span>)</span>\napp.include_router(...)\napp.add_middleware(...)\n</code></pre></div><p>So <strong><code>app</code> is the central application object.</strong></p><hr><h1>Step 8 — Create our first endpoint</h1><p>Now add:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.get(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/health\"</span></span>)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">health_check</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> {<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"status\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>}\n</code></pre></div><p>Your complete <code>main.py</code> should now be:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> fastapi <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.get(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/health\"</span></span>)</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">health_check</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> {<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"status\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>}\n</code></pre></div><p>Don't add anything else yet.</p><hr><h1>Understand this code</h1><p>This part:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.get(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/health\"</span></span>)</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>is a <strong>decorator</strong>.</p><p>It tells FastAPI:</p><blockquote><p>\"When someone sends a GET request to <code>/health</code>, run the function immediately below.\"</p></blockquote><p>The function is:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">health_check</span>():\n</code></pre></div><p>And it returns:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">{<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"status\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>}\n</code></pre></div><p>FastAPI will automatically turn that Python dictionary into a JSON response.</p><p>So:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">GET /health\n      ↓\nFastAPI finds matching route\n      ↓\nhealth_check()\n      ↓\n{\"status\": \"ok\"}\n      ↓\nJSON response\n</code></pre></div><hr><h1>Step 9 — Start the server</h1><p>Save <code>main.py</code>.</p><p>In the terminal, run:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">bash</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-bash hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">fastapi dev main.py\n</code></pre></div><p>You should see FastAPI start a development server.</p><p>You should get an address similar to:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">http://127.0.0.1:8000\n</code></pre></div><p><strong>Do not close this terminal.</strong></p><hr><h1>Step 10 — Test our API</h1><p>Open your browser and go to:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">http://127.0.0.1:8000/health\n</code></pre></div><p>You should get:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">json</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-json hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"status\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>🎉 <strong>You just created your first FastAPI endpoint.</strong></p><hr><h1>Step 11 — Open Swagger</h1><p>Now go to:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs\n</code></pre></div><p>You should see Swagger UI.</p><p>You should see something similar to:</p><p><br></p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">GET\n/health\n</code></pre></div><p>Click:</p><p><strong>GET <code>/health</code> → Try it out → Execute</strong></p><p>You should get:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">200\n</code></pre></div><p>and:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">json</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-json hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-attr\">\"status\"</span><span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>This is one of FastAPI's major features: it automatically generates interactive API documentation from your application and type/schema information.</p><hr><h1>🧠 Stop and understand the architecture</h1><p>We currently have:</p><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">text</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-text hljs language-plaintext\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">Browser / Swagger\n       │\n       │ GET /health\n       ↓\n   Uvicorn\n       │\n       ↓\n    FastAPI\n       │\n       ↓\n @app.get(\"/health\")\n       │\n       ↓\n health_check()\n       │\n       ↓\n {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n       │\n       ↓\n     JSON\n</code></pre></div><p>There are <strong>several different things here</strong>, and later we'll understand exactly how each layer works.</p><p>For now, remember:</p><h3>Uvicorn</h3><p>Runs our application server.</p><h3>FastAPI</h3><p>Our web framework/application.</p><h3>Route</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">@app.get(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-string\">\"/health\"</span></span>)</span>\n</code></pre></div><p>Connects an HTTP request to Python code.</p><h3>Function</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">health_check</span>():\n</code></pre></div><p>Contains the logic.</p><h3>Return value</h3><div class=\"code-block-wrapper\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span class=\"code-lang-label\">python</span><button class=\"copy-code-btn\">Copy</button><pre><code class=\"language-python hljs\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-highlighted=\"yes\">{<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"status\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"ok\"</span>}\n</code></pre></div><p>Becomes the HTTP response.</p><hr><h2>✅ Part 1 Progress</h2><ul><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Create project</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Create virtual environment</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Activate environment</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Install FastAPI</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Create <code>main.py</code></p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Create FastAPI application</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Create first GET route</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Start server</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Test endpoint</p></li><li><p><input disabled=\"\" checked=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Open Swagger</p></li></ul><h3>Next</h3><p><strong>Part 2 → Routes, HTTP methods, paths, path parameters, query parameters, and request/response fundamentals.</strong></p><p>But first, <strong>actually do these steps in VS Code</strong>.</p><p>Once <code>/health</code> works and you can see it in <code>/docs</code>, reply <strong><code>done</code></strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>main&nbsp; &nbsp;→ main.py</p><p>:app&nbsp; &nbsp;→ app = FastAPI()</p><p>--reload → code change hone par server automatically restart</p><p><br></p><p>in</p>",
